WEBVTT

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:04.350
<i>In just another second,</i>

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:07.230
<i>the broadcast tower would 
be back under their control.</i>

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.920
<i>But a surprise attack by the 
terraformars changes the situation.</i>

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.150
<i>Wolf and the other civilians 
can't do their jobs,</i>

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:16.030
<i>and are left with nothing but despair.</i>

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.460
<i>But there was a single, faint sigh.</i>

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:21.960
<i>Amelia Venkatesh.</i>

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:26.620
<i>Her thin, trembling fingers 
tried their best to create hope.</i>

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:29.420
<i>For her comrades who were waiting,</i>

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:33.010
<i>and for Keiji, who protected her.</i>

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:41.570
<i>I won't let it go to waste, everyone.</i>

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:47.050
<i>You did a great job getting us this far,</i>

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:49.900
<i>Wolf...</i>

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:56.790
<i>And you, Keiji, fought until 
you could barely stand...</i>

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:08.590
<i>I won't let it go to waste!</i>

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:44.230
<i>What will you do</i>

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:47.700
<i>if we can't get communications back online?</i>

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:53.010
All our efforts will go to waste.

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:55.760
Our vast...

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.990
efforts.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:03.120
I believe that they will do it.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:07.360
12 Second Revolution

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:17.050
Ryuichi, get a thread up to the top...

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:19.220
I can't!

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.290
I can only fire them once!

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:24.180
That's why I'm rank 70!

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:26.900
I'll...

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:34.940
<i>I-It's no good.</i>

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:38.750
<i>I've passed the limit of how long I 
can handle the poison a long time ago.</i>

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:41.970
<i>We'll all die.</i>

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:46.640
<i>Keiji... who spent all his energy...</i>

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:48.300
<i>...is about to die!</i>

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:01.540
Damn it!

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:04.220
I'm not dying here!

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:21.610
Man that hissing's annoying.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:24.570
Is this the time to be laughing, Akari?

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:27.110
Keep your promise.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:32.260
You made a big promise to that young boy.

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:34.420
If you can't keep it, I'll kill you.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:38.960
I'm Harukaze Sakurato.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:47.190
We're going to Mars to find 
a way to treat your illness.

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:47.970
Really?

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:50.310
Leave it to me!

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:53.480
I can believe you and wait, right?

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:56.060
I'll keep that promise, no matter what.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:57.540
Good!

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:02.470
<i>Everyone's fighting.</i>

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:04.370
<i>So are they...</i>

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:19.450
<i>I won't let it go to waste.</i>

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:22.170
<i>No matter what!</i>

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:24.950
<b>M.A.R.S. Ranking 77
Amelia Venkatesh
US-Japan Joint No. 2 Division
Surgery Base: Narwhal</b>

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:33.700
<i>I don't need anything but my eyes, fingers,</i>

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:35.980
<i>and brain right now.</i>

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:42.520
<i>The whale dives deep, and for a long time.</i>

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:47.650
<i>When it does, it shuts off 
organs it doesn't need.</i>

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:51.740
<i>Amelia has also shut down most of her organs.</i>

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:05.800
Hey, why are you running?

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:12.900
Everybody's having a party.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:21.940
I've been running for an hour now.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.170
They must've forgotten me.

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:27.590
You're always like that.

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:30.290
You don't slack off even 
during harsh training.

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:32.450
How can you do all that?

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:38.070
Why?

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:41.380
Is it just a habit?

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:46.200
Or is it like, 
"Putting forth effort is important"?

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:48.830
I don't know.

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:52.710
I'm not interested in the effort itself.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.680
How far I've run,

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.430
how much I've lifted...

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:58.360
If you put too much of a 
priority on the process,

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:01.810
you become satisfied with that and 
lose sight of your original goal.

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:03.560
That's dangerous.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:06.280
Then, why?

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:10.690
When I became the world champion...

00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:12.610
What? World champion?

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:16.840
Sorry, I underestimated you.

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:18.330
It's fine.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:22.420
It was a close thing.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:26.590
I won by a referee's call, 
in a very close fight.

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:31.730
That was the first time all the 
training I'd done had a meaning.

00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:33.760
It had a meaning?

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:38.970
I train so when it just takes a little 
extra, I have a little extra to give.

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:44.440
I don't know if running will 
help with my mission on Mars,

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:46.550
but I think it's so that someday,

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:49.650
when the time comes for that 
little extra, it's there.

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:55.050
Well, I'd like to participate 
in the next party.

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:57.870
If you want it...

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:07.520
It's good.

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:15.940
<i>So this is the last thing I remember?</i>

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:18.060
<i>It figures.</i>

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:26.730
<i>I love you, Keiji.</i>

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:29.670
<i>I don't want to die.</i>

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:31.690
<i>I don't want to die!</i>

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:52.200
<i>But it's all just so frustrating...</i>

00:08:54.270 --> 00:08:56.290
<i>Keiji protected us.</i>

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:59.560
<i>Erika brought us here.</i>

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:04.250
<i>Wolf and the others accomplished so much...</i>

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:11.730
<i>All it takes is a little extra, 
and I've got nothing more to give.</i>

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:15.770
<i>It's so frustrating!</i>

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:21.330
<i>Keiji, I understand now.</i>

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:24.840
<i>There was a meaning in the 
way you were always running.</i>

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:27.870
<i>There was a meaning in the way Wolf didn't</i>

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:31.340
<i>quit being an engineer, 
even when he was faced with failure.</i>

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:34.310
<i>I'll create it...</i>

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:39.180
<i>I'll grab it...</i>

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:44.550
<i>...that "little extra" you all gave...</i>

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:46.600
<i>And then...</i>

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:49.310
<i>And then...</i>

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:55.130
<i>We can say there's a meaning 
in the battle we fought,</i>

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:57.150
<i>right?</i>

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:06.290
<i>Once I push this button,</i>

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:08.830
<i>tell me I did good,</i>

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:10.750
<i>Keiji...</i>

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:38.600
Michelle-san, was that?

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:48.750
General Liu, this is...

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.590
<i>This is not good.</i>

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:51.710
<i>Did they get us?</i>

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:55.270
<i>It'll take 10 seconds for 
the support program to boot up.</i>

00:11:05.150 --> 00:11:06.810
<i>I think it's so that someday,</i>

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:09.150
<i>when the time comes for that 
little extra, it's there.</i>

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:13.190
<i>I have to tell them...</i>

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:17.190
<i>I have to say it.</i>

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:21.860
<i>I have to restore my lungs and throat.</i>

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:35.340
Keiji... Everyone...

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:48.600
We've got it! It's from 
the Annex I control room!

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:50.830
We know the situation.

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:52.840
They should try to tell us what's going on.

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:54.750
Don't miss a word.

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:58.720
Say it! Say it! Say it!

00:11:59.070 --> 00:11:59.780
Say it!

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:07.410
<i>Save us...</i>

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:08.870
<i>Save us...</i>

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:14.490
<i>It's no good.</i>

00:12:14.490 --> 00:12:18.750
<i>She didn't say what we needed to hear.</i>

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:23.510
<i>That was the only communication we 
received from Annex I to U-NASA HQ.</i>

00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:26.460
<i>We didn't get what we needed.</i>

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:29.060
<i>It was just a scream for a help.</i>

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:31.020
<i>Save us...</i>

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:32.370
¡Sí!

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:32.770
Da!

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:33.310
Ja!

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:33.980
Yes!

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:34.940
Understood!

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:41.030
<b>Annex Project
A Mars expedition plan that would involve the 
creation of a vaccine for the 100% lethal AE Virus, 
and the recovery of 100 Terraformar bodies as samples. 
100 crew were sent in a large manned ship, the Annex 1, in 2620.</b>

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:45.800
<i>Keiji...</i>

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:47.370
<i>Everyone...</i>

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:50.830
<i>I can't walk another step...</i>

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:52.330
Save us...

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:54.750
<i>But once I've said this, 
I'll go to be with you.</i>

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:57.460
<i>Let me be with you forever...</i>

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:58.250
Save us...

00:12:58.250 --> 00:12:59.840
<i>Let me stay with you forever...</i>

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:03.770
Jared!

00:13:03.770 --> 00:13:04.970
Is Amelia the last one?

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:07.160
Yeah! Hurry!

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:08.710
I can hear it!

00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:11.770
They're here! A huge army of terraformars!

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:26.000
Three ships?

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:26.860
What's wrong?

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:28.110
It was only for a minute,

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:30.280
but we got observation data 
from the broadcast terror.

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:33.720
It says that No. 4 Branch Office's 
heavily armed rescue ship

00:13:33.720 --> 00:13:36.870
is heading to Mars far faster than 
the published information says.

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:38.250
What?

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:39.480
That's not all.

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:40.420
There are two more ships.

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:44.590
There are three ships heading 
to Mars in secret right now!

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:49.830
Communications with Earth seem to have been 
reestablished, if only for a few seconds.

00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:54.350
It's possible that continuing the original 
mission plan has become difficult.

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:57.780
Bring back the First and the Second 
even if you have to kill them,

00:13:57.780 --> 00:13:59.690
and gather at the designated point.

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:02.740
We leave Mars immediately.

00:14:06.510 --> 00:14:07.800
Did our communications...

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:11.310
They were back online, 
but went down soon after.

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:13.830
Then everyone...

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:15.390
I don't know.

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:18.500
Either a program to block 
the hacking booted up,

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:19.730
or...

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:21.800
Let's go back, Michelle-san.

00:14:21.800 --> 00:14:23.800
If something happened at the Annex...

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:27.680
No, the captain's orders 
were to head to the north.

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:30.890
We'll believe in everyone until the end.

00:14:35.630 --> 00:14:37.560
You're not in heaven.

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:39.020
Jared?

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:41.770
I-If this isn't heaven, where am I?

00:14:42.570 --> 00:14:45.560
The poison made me unable to even...

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:50.960
She had an antidote.

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:53.280
She created it from her own body, supposedly.

00:14:54.050 --> 00:14:56.320
It's a powerful poison,

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:59.720
so just one injection won't fully heal you,

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:01.760
but she gave it to us without any trouble.

00:15:07.870 --> 00:15:10.520
Annex 1 has been taken over.

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:12.340
No.

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:15.060
You could say it's being dismantled.

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:19.430
They poured in at an incredible 
rate, in huge numbers.

00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:22.490
It was right after we heard 
a terraformar broadcast

00:15:22.490 --> 00:15:24.700
inside the ship for some reason.

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:27.720
I don't know what they 
said in their language.

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:31.820
Maybe they said that the poison 
had started to dissipate.

00:15:32.350 --> 00:15:37.300
Maybe they decided there was 
no need to be careful with how

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:38.880
they treated the Annex itself.

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:40.080
Captain,

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:43.600
th-that's not what I want to know...

00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:45.380
Why I'm alive,

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:47.230
and what happened with the terraformars,

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:49.090
that doesn't matter.

00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:52.620
I don't remember saying 
everything I needed to.

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:54.620
I did my best, but...

00:15:55.520 --> 00:15:57.450
It didn't work!

00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:04.310
You were only able to talk 
for about ten seconds, right?

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:08.030
During that time, you connected 
to America or Japan.

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:12.580
At the same time, the officer's 
radio came back online

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:15.440
and we were able to hear everything.

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:19.580
Those two did it.

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:24.120
German Branch Office, can you hear us?

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:26.530
No. 4 Division has betrayed us!

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:30.300
Send reinforcements! I am Michelle K. Davis!

00:16:30.850 --> 00:16:33.880
Share this information with 
all the branch offices!

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:41.810
That ten seconds you civilians 
sacrificed your lives to bring us

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:45.600
changed the destiny of 
this planet and saved us.

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:48.320
Thank you, Amelia.

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:50.260
You did well.

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:55.570
Thank you, Keiji, Wolf, 
Erika, Ryuichi, Ryuji!

00:16:56.090 --> 00:16:58.430
We went after Akari and Michelle, but we

00:16:58.430 --> 00:17:01.160
ran into the terraformars and were delayed.

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:06.130
We decided to give up on chasing them 
and went back to pick up you civilians.

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:10.750
And then they ran into us as we 
fled Annex 1 on the air bikes.

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:16.410
Many of our comrades lost their lives,

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:18.920
but the mission was a success.

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:22.100
Everyone, you did an amazing job.

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:55.260
Hong there barely knows 
anything about the operation,

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:59.050
but Xi Chun-Li should know how to 
get in touch with her comrades.

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:00.810
When she wakes up,

00:18:00.810 --> 00:18:03.440
I'll have her get in touch with Liu 
via the air bike's communicators.

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:07.020
And tell him that his plan's been found out.

00:18:07.710 --> 00:18:09.700
That will bring an end to this battle.

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:11.980
It should.

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:15.250
There's no reason to fight any longer.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:19.670
What? How very sad.

00:18:19.670 --> 00:18:23.700
If that's true, I can 
only describe it as sad.

00:18:24.150 --> 00:18:26.550
Our goal, our desire, does not change.

00:18:27.440 --> 00:18:29.630
Even if we can't get back to Earth,

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:32.840
we won't let you have Hizamaru Akari.

00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:34.920
I just got it.

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:37.270
Inputting Unit 1's positioning coordinates.

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:42.830
Now!

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:45.770
Fire the missile at Hizamaru Akari.

00:18:48.880 --> 00:18:50.520
Not happening.

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:53.440
This ends here.

00:19:02.930 --> 00:19:06.270
We're through the worst of it, for now.

00:19:07.820 --> 00:19:09.040
Yeah.

00:19:09.270 --> 00:19:10.780
This is the

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:14.880
first time in my life I'm 
really glad to be alive.

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:17.300
You, too, Michelle-san?

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:19.450
I wonder why, huh?

00:19:19.450 --> 00:19:20.530
Sheesh...

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:24.780
I hope this helps him get better.

00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:27.690
Sakurato?

00:19:27.690 --> 00:19:29.450
Was that his name?

00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:34.240
I'm glad that we were 
able to keep hope alive.

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:36.110
Michelle-san.

00:19:37.180 --> 00:19:38.770
Can I let you handle the controls?

00:19:38.770 --> 00:19:39.910
Oh, sure.

00:19:39.910 --> 00:19:43.070
Sorry, I need to rest.

00:19:46.730 --> 00:19:48.540
She falls asleep fast.

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:52.620
But she's really cute right now.

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:57.000
I'm not asleep yet.

00:19:57.300 --> 00:19:59.280
Why not?

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:00.770
Is that my fault?

00:20:00.770 --> 00:20:02.150
No, go to sleep.

00:20:02.150 --> 00:20:05.480
I'm so jealous they get to be in love...

00:20:10.830 --> 00:20:14.160
I believe we'll all be 
able to reunite safely,

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:17.360
but if something happens and 
we can't gather at Annex 1,

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:18.630
run to the north.

00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:21.400
If there is any hope, it's there.

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:29.410
Captain, where are we going?

00:20:29.900 --> 00:20:31.560
Right... To the north!

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:34.240
Head to the north!

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:36.380
We're going to the sea!

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:42.300
To the sea!

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:00.840
Oh, come on!

00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:03.690
That's why I told you not 
to buy a classic car.

00:21:03.690 --> 00:21:04.670
Wait, wait.

00:21:04.670 --> 00:21:05.690
There's a village up ahead.

00:21:05.690 --> 00:21:08.370
Let's ask directions. 
There may be a place we can stay.

00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:24.300
What's with them?

00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:25.530
That's not English, is it?

00:21:25.530 --> 00:21:26.790
What language is it?

00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:28.230
Oh, no. Let's go back.

00:21:28.230 --> 00:21:29.290
Those are illegal immigrants.

00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:31.580
You read about them on the 
internet all the time lately.

00:21:31.580 --> 00:21:34.060
They squat in abandon villages.

00:21:34.540 --> 00:21:36.870
They don't speak our language 
and there's no telling what they'll do.

00:21:36.870 --> 00:21:38.020
Let's just run!

00:22:05.730 --> 00:22:08.070
I'll leave some curry for you.

00:22:08.070 --> 00:22:09.680
Eat it while it's hot.

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:12.680
<b>Stay out!</b>

00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:15.990
You didn't even take the 
exams this year, did you?

00:22:17.430 --> 00:22:20.690
Your uncle in Yamanashi says 
he'll find you a job...

00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:23.270
That's right!

00:22:23.270 --> 00:22:25.120
You're going to be a lawyer, right?

00:22:25.950 --> 00:22:29.090
I'm sorry to bother you 
when you're studying...

00:23:02.250 --> 00:23:07.010
<b>New Tokyo Expressway
500 Year Anniversary</b>

00:23:12.020 --> 00:23:14.440
This'll be a melee fights.

00:23:15.950 --> 00:23:17.650
We'll need more fighters.

00:23:19.610 --> 00:23:24.400
As many anti-terraformar 
experts as we can find.

00:23:26.070 --> 00:23:27.570
Come back!

00:23:29.500 --> 00:23:31.890
I won't lose to my illness.

00:23:32.280 --> 00:23:33.480
So...

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:36.350
please be safe...

00:23:37.050 --> 00:23:38.540
Hizamaru-san.
